But can she really handle it?

271
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,570
Class meeting lasts a whole hour.

272
00:15:06,970 --> 00:15:10,220
She can barely handle
the morning assembly.

273
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:16,370
E-everyone, 

274
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,870
class meeting

275
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:22,910
starts now.

276
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,420
SCARED
F… funeral?

277
00:15:24,410 --> 00:15:25,870
SCARED
She definitely said funeral.

278
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:29,210
The scary class meeting

279
00:15:29,210 --> 00:15:30,910
FUNERAL CLASS MEETING
begins.

280
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,670
SHIVERING

281
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:34,180
This is a hellish start.

282
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:36,970
Everyone looks terrified.

283
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,870
Her handwriting is all wobbly.

284
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,810
She seems more nervous than usual.

285
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:43,210
What is that? Sutras?

286
00:15:43,210 --> 00:15:45,070
Are we at a living funeral?

287
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:48,220
This isn't class meeting anymore.

288
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:51,570
Her face is a bit red.

289
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,660
Is she still not recovering

290
00:15:52,670 --> 00:15:54,230
from the running this morning?

291
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,730
HEART RACING

292
00:16:03,950 --> 00:16:04,950
SPLITS

293
00:16:08,570 --> 00:16:10,570
Kowakowa-sensei…

294
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:12,920
She's holding a utility knife.

295
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:13,920
Is she

296
00:16:16,170 --> 00:16:17,720
MENACING
charging up

297
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,020
to attack us?

298
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:21,070
Kowakowa-sensei doesn't throw chalk, 

299
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:22,970
and she throws utility knives?

300
00:16:22,970 --> 00:16:25,370
She definitely doesn't have
the strength for that.

301
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,070
She must have a reason for not moving.

302
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:33,230
This is my first class meeting.

303
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,820
Sensei, I want to be class president.

304
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:41,270
The first class meeting
of the new semester

305
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:42,970
will elect a class president, right?

306
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:48,520
Then I'll take charge from here on out.

307
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,170
This is agonizing.

308
00:16:50,170 --> 00:16:52,520
This position is not mediocre at all.

309
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:54,970
Sensei, are you okay?

310
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:56,870
A… Abikura-kun.

311
00:16:56,870 --> 00:16:58,420
Uh…

312
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:01,920
Could you help me get unstuck?

313
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,220
It's caught.

314
00:17:09,810 --> 00:17:11,770
She's not wearing underwear.

315
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:17,010
I overslept this morning
and forgot to put it on.

316
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:19,069
Does that really happen?

317
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,119
No.

318
00:17:20,109 --> 00:17:22,810
Judging by how flustered she was
this morning, it's definitely possible.

319
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:25,170
My leg also cramped up.

320
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:29,610
But touching the teacher's stockings
in front of the whole class…

321
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:31,070
Abikura-kun.

322
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:35,620
This is my first class meeting.

323
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:38,330
I don't want it to end in failure.

324
00:17:39,310 --> 00:17:41,410
I… I'll help you now.

325
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:42,910
SHOCKED

326
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:45,920
DEAD SILENCE

327
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:49,310
FORCING COMPOSURE
Let's continue with the class meeting.

328
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:53,320
CLASS 2-2

329
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,860
Hey, class president.

330
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,770
Do my homework for me.

331
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:57,730
Shut up.

332
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,520
Although it was to help sensei, 

333
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,820
I ended up becoming class president.

334
00:18:03,810 --> 00:18:08,210
My perfectly ordinary school life
is crumbling.

335
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:13,170
What's this?

336
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:15,110
A challenge letter?

337
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,820
To Abikura-kun, 

338
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:20,720
I would like to discuss
class management policies with you.

339
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,420
Could you please stay after school?

340
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:26,870
A private talk with sensei?

341
00:18:27,370 --> 00:18:29,380
Long live the class president!

342
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,170
A… Abikura-kun.

343
00:18:32,170 --> 00:18:34,170
Thank you for coming.

344
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:35,620
A megaphone?

345
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,770
Um… Sensei…

346
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,470
Aren't we supposed to discuss
class management policies?

347
00:18:40,470 --> 00:18:43,120
Y… yes, that's right.

348
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:45,770
But at the faculty meeting today…

349
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:47,910
Hiwamura-sensei, 

350
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:49,970
your volume makes it a bit hard
to hear you clearly.

351
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:52,310
Doesn't that affect your teaching?

352
00:18:52,310 --> 00:18:53,870
CRUSHED

353
00:18:53,870 --> 00:18:55,570
That hit the nail on the head.

354
00:18:55,570 --> 00:19:00,420
So I thought this would
help my voice carry.

355
00:19:02,610 --> 00:19:04,360
She's trying hard, 

356
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:07,660
but increasing the volume
doesn't make her words any clearer.

357
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:09,210
I think it's a good idea.

358
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:11,260
The main reason everyone is afraid of you

359
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:14,270
is that there's a communication issue.

360
00:19:14,810 --> 00:19:17,360
E… everyone is afraid of me?

361
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:20,910
She didn't realize?

362
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:24,120
Have I made them scared?

363
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,860
My… my heart aches.

364
00:19:27,210 --> 00:19:29,160
No wonder.

365
00:19:29,170 --> 00:19:34,170
I thought everyone seemed
to be avoiding my gaze.

366
00:19:34,170 --> 00:19:35,120
Huh?

367
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:38,980
But Abikura-kun, 
you can communicate normally with me.

368
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:39,480
STARTLED

369
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:40,670
Well…

370
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:42,870
Come to think of it, 

371
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:49,270
I heard you weren't particularly active
in your first year.

372
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:52,370
But you volunteered to be class president.

373
00:19:52,370 --> 00:19:53,570
Even though you were scared, 

374
00:19:53,570 --> 00:19:56,370
you still came to talk to me.

375
00:19:56,370 --> 00:19:59,010
That's amazing. I respect that.

376
00:19:59,010 --> 00:20:01,960
I… I feel like there's
a strange misunderstanding.

377
00:20:01,970 --> 00:20:05,470
Anyway, the megaphone is a good idea.

378
00:20:05,470 --> 00:20:10,110
Just try to speak slowly
and enunciate each word clearly.

379
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:11,820
I… I see.

380
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:17,360
W… water striders are red.

381
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:19,020
Great, I heard that clearly!

382
00:20:19,610 --> 00:20:22,160
R… really?

383
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:27,260
Th… then if I stand on the podium, 
will students in back rows hear me clearly?

384
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:34,010
Water strider.

385
00:20:34,010 --> 00:20:35,920
I can hear you. Super clear!

386
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:37,430
OVERJOYED

387
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:41,960
Th… this way, they won't be
afraid of me anymore, right?

388
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:43,810
Definitely!

389
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:47,460
Can my thoughts really reach them?

390
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:48,880
They absolutely can!

391
00:20:50,270 --> 00:20:51,670
Abikura-kun.

392
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:54,540
Did my feelings reach you?

393
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,960
HEART RACING
Yes!

394
00:20:57,370 --> 00:20:58,750
What are we doing?

395
00:21:01,270 --> 00:21:02,520
Thank you.

396
00:21:02,910 --> 00:21:06,420
You're always helping me.

397
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:09,420
Not really, I haven't done much.

398
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:13,260
I just happened to
witness her trying her best.

399
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:17,930
HEART RACING
I might actually be falling for her.

400
00:21:20,660 --> 00:21:22,710
But I'm feeling a bit tired.

401
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:23,980
FALLING

402
00:21:25,370 --> 00:21:26,960
The megaphone fell!

403
00:21:26,970 --> 00:21:30,720
That's an important tool for Sensei
to communicate with the students.

404
00:21:34,810 --> 00:21:38,160
S-sorry, Abikura-kun.

405
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:40,540
I-it's okay. It was my fault.

406
00:21:40,530 --> 00:21:41,150
TREMBLING
I-it's okay. It was my fault.

407
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:41,660
STARTLED

408
00:21:42,610 --> 00:21:44,420
I-I'll get up right away.

409
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:45,370
Wait.

410
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:48,760
P-please don't talk right now.

411
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:54,970
We didn't discuss class management at all.

412
00:21:54,970 --> 00:21:57,270
Let's discuss it another time.

413
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,060
Abikura-kun.

414
00:22:01,270 --> 00:22:03,510
You're my ideal class president.

415
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:06,070
Let's do our best together.

416
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:07,460
Okay.

417
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:10,020
The strange misunderstanding continues.
